  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Transformer Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Transformer Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Block Stack",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Stack of ==identical blocks==: **self-attention** then **feed-forward network**",
                "Each sublayer wrapped in ==residual connection== + **layer norm**",
                "Embeddings turn ==token IDs== into vectors",
                "==Positional information== is added so word order is not lost"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Embed + position",
                    "sub": "IDs to vectors",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Block × N",
                    "sub": "attention + FFN",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Project",
                    "sub": "final vector",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Logits",
                    "sub": "score per vocab token",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each block ==refines== the vector of every token",
                "Last layer's vector → **logits** over the vocabulary"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Decoder vs Encoder",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Decoder-only",
                "Encoder-only"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Examples",
                  "GPT, Claude, Llama",
                  "BERT"
                ],
                [
                  "Reads",
                  "left to right",
                  "both directions"
                ],
                [
                  "Used for",
                  "generating text",
                  "understanding tasks"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Transformer vs RNN",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "RNN: tokens processed ==sequentially==",
                "Transformer: ==all tokens in parallel== during training"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Parallel training on all tokens is why transformers beat RNNs and could scale."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tokens and Next-Token Prediction",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Tokens and Next-Token Prediction",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a token is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Token== = sub-word chunk; **BPE** merges frequent byte pairs",
                "About ==4 characters== or ==0.75 English words== per token",
                "Tokenizing is a {blue:deterministic} text → ID map, done before the model",
                "Model sees IDs only, never raw characters"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The generation loop",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Logits",
                    "note": "score per vocab token",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Softmax",
                    "note": "probabilities",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Sample",
                    "note": "pick one token",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Append",
                    "note": "to the input",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Repeat",
                    "note": "until stop token",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Knob",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Temperature",
                  "rescales logits: low = near-greedy, high = diverse"
                ],
                [
                  "top-k",
                  "keep the k likeliest tokens"
                ],
                [
                  "top-p",
                  "keep smallest set with mass ≥ p"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Where it breaks",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Letter counting: the word is split into odd chunks",
                "Arithmetic: numbers split unevenly",
                "Non-English text: many tokens per word"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "top-k and top-p ==cut candidates== first, then one token is sampled. Generation is **autoregressive**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Attention Mechanism",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Attention Mechanism",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Scores, Scaling and Masking",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Each token makes a ==Query==, a ==Key== and a ==Value== vector",
                "Scores = `softmax(QKᵀ/√d)`",
                "Output = **weighted sum of Values**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "QKᵀ",
                    "sub": "raw scores",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "÷ √d",
                    "sub": "scale down",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Causal mask",
                    "sub": "hide later tokens",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Softmax",
                    "sub": "weights",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "× V",
                    "sub": "weighted sum",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`÷√d` keeps dot products small, so softmax does not ==saturate== and kill gradients",
                "{red:Causal mask}: a token cannot attend to later tokens, so ==next-token training== is valid"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Heads, Cost and Cache",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "What it does",
                "Why it matters"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Multi-head**",
                  "Several attentions in parallel, then concatenated",
                  "Heads learn different relations"
                ],
                [
                  "**Cost**",
                  "Grows as ==n²== with sequence length",
                  "Root of long-context expense"
                ],
                [
                  "**KV cache**",
                  "Stores past Keys and Values",
                  "One step per new token, no recompute"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Generation",
              "text": "Only the new token needs a fresh Query; its Keys and Values join the ==cache==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Context Windows in Practice",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Context Windows in Practice",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Window Budget",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Context window== = max tokens of input + output the model attends to at once",
                "Over the limit: input is **truncated** or the call {red:errors}",
                "Input and output ==share== the window, so a long prompt shrinks the answer room"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Input",
                    "sub": "prompt + history",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Output",
                    "sub": "room left",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Window",
                    "sub": "input + output",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Resent Every Turn",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==No memory== between calls",
                "The whole conversation is **resent** each turn, and you pay for it each time",
                "{red:Lost in the middle}: long prompts are recalled worse mid-prompt"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Position in prompt",
                "Recall"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Start",
                  "{green:strong}"
                ],
                [
                  "Middle",
                  "{red:weak}"
                ],
                [
                  "End",
                  "{green:strong}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Window vs Retrieval",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Bigger window is **not** a substitute for ==retrieval==",
                "Long inputs cost more, run slower, dilute attention",
                "==Prompt caching== reuses a repeated prefix: lower latency and cost"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Order the prompt",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "System rules",
                    "note": "stable",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Reference docs",
                    "note": "stable",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "New question",
                    "note": "changes",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Stable first",
              "text": "Put ==stable content first==, changing content last, so the cached prefix matches."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pretraining, Instruction Tuning and RLHF",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Pretraining, Instruction Tuning and RLHF",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Three Stages",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Pretraining",
                    "note": "next-token prediction on huge raw text → base model: completes text, ignores instructions",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "SFT",
                    "note": "fine-tune on prompt-response pairs → follows instructions, desired format",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RLHF / DPO",
                    "note": "preference tuning → helpful, safe",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Stage",
                "Gives"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Pretraining",
                  "==knowledge=="
                ],
                [
                  "SFT",
                  "==format== and behavior"
                ],
                [
                  "RLHF / DPO",
                  "==helpfulness and safety==, **no new facts**"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. RLHF vs DPO",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Humans rank outputs",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Reward model",
                    "sub": "learns preferences",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "PPO-style RL",
                    "sub": "optimizes the model",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==DPO== skips the separate reward model",
                "Trains directly on **preference pairs**",
                "Simpler and more stable than PPO"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Expecting a **base model** to chat: it just continues text",
                "Assuming fine-tuning reliably teaches **new knowledge**",
                "==Reward hacking==: the model games the reward model"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Facts come from ==pretraining==. SFT and RLHF only shape **behavior**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
